{"ref":"BDB, חֵ֫צִי","hw":"חֵ֫צִי","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">חֵ֫צִי</span></big>  <strong>n.m.</strong> <sup><a data-ref=\"II Kings 9:24\" href=\"/II_Kings.9.24\">2 K 9:24</a></sup> <strong>arrow (</strong>cf. Arabic <span dir=\"rtl\">حَظْوَةٌ</span> / <span dir=\"rtl\">حُظْوَةٌ</span>, Ethiopic ሐጸ: <em>id.</em>, Di <sup>134</sup>, and v. Dr on <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 20:36\" href=\"/I_Samuel.20.36\">1 S 20:36</a><strong>)</strong>—abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">הַחֵ֫צִי</span> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 20:36\" href=\"/I_Samuel.20.36\">1 S 20:36</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 20:37\" href=\"/I_Samuel.20.37\">37</a><sup>(×2)</sup> + v <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 20:38\" href=\"/I_Samuel.20.38\">38</a> Kt (Qr <span dir=\"rtl\">הַחִצִּים</span>), perhaps also v <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 20:21\" href=\"/I_Samuel.20.21\">21</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 20:22\" href=\"/I_Samuel.20.22\">22</a> (so 𝔊 We, for MT pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">הַחִצִּים</span>), <a data-ref=\"II Kings 9:24\" href=\"/II_Kings.9.24\">2 K 9:24</a>; the usual form is <span dir=\"rtl\">חֵץ</span>; v. infr.","next":"BDB, יַחְצְאֵל","prev":"BDB, חֲצִי הַמְּנֻחוֹת"}